# The bytes a release froze, one line each as sha256sum writes it: the
# SHA-256, two spaces, the path from the repository's root. checks/frozen.sh
# fails when a file listed here is gone or holds other bytes, so what version 1
# froze cannot be edited in place by a later commit (STORAGE.md §4.2, §4.4,
# §6, §15.3). A path followed by `#` and a statement's name is one row of
# queries/signatures.json, the line stating that name: a row may be added by
# a minor version, and a frozen one never moves.
#
# Empty while every part is a draft. The commit releasing a part adds, with
# `bash checks/frozen.sh . --digest <path...>`:
#
# storage-v1.0.0
#   migrations/storage/0001_init.sql
#   payloads/*.v1.schema.json
#   queries/signatures.json#storage/* (every row of the three directories)
# sync-v1.0.0
#   nothing of its own: its seam is prose and vectors, which checks/tags.sh
#   holds to the tag
# search-v1.0.0, later
#   migrations/search/0001_init.sql
#   queries/signatures.json#search/* (every row)
#
# A line leaves this file only in the commit of the minor version removing
# its statement, which lists it (STORAGE.md §4.4).
